ntdll: timer reuse window 10 s; registry key and value notes for FEX.

Timer reuse (0010) kept a timer only when the thread that made it closed it within 100 ms.
In b159 (d2r9) 78 timers a second were reused, and about 10 a second met every other rule
but were closed later than that (tm_too_old). The window decides nothing about what is safe:
the rules that do (same thread, every setting seen to fire, no APC or period, never
cancelled, duplicated or used by another thread) are the same at any age; the window only
keeps handles that live long out of the pool. It is now 10 s, set with
WINE_D2R_TIMER_LIFE_MS (1 to 3,600,000 ms; 100 gives d2r9's behaviour). tm_too_old now
counts timers closed later than the window.

In b159 one unnamed thread of D2R's process (tid 784, ~1% CPU, started before t=15) sent
open_key ~80 and get_key_value ~60 times a second; nothing says which key. NtOpenKeyEx and
NtQueryValueKey now note each call for FEX, appended to __wine_d2r_server_calls_ext at byte
2176: reg_open_next and reg_value_next (u64: calls noted so far; the latest is entry
(next - 1) % 8 resp. % 4), then reg_open[8] and reg_value[4] at byte 2192, 128 bytes each:
seq (u32, odd while being written, +2 per write; a reader takes seq, copies, and keeps the
copy when seq was even and the same after an acquire fence), tid (u32, caller), status
(u32, NTSTATUS), name_len (u32, characters), parent (u64: root directory handle, or the key
handle for a value read), result (u64: the key handle opened, 0 for value reads), name (96
bytes: key path relative to parent or value name, ASCII with '?' for other characters, NUL
terminated, cut to 95). A thread finding the note it would write already being written
leaves it to that one. The export grows from 2,176 to 3,728 bytes (466 ULONG64); size (byte
48) says 3,728. Version stays 1. On with the request counts (WINE_D2R_CALL_COUNTS).

Tests: the 0010 model test with this sync.c (200 seeds x 3: default window, tiny pools, and
a 1 ms window), every result compared with WINE_D2R_TIMER_REUSE=0: 600 runs, 0 differences;
kept timers 159,377 with the 10 s window, 45,190 with 1 ms. The note writer, compiled from
registry.c, with four threads writing as fast as they can and a reader using the rule above:
17 million notes each, 0 torn copies kept; names longer than 95 characters are cut, non-ASCII
characters become '?'.
---
diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/sync.c b/dlls/ntdll/sync.c
index f33d9b3..81aac10 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/sync.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/sync.c
@@ -861,7 +861,7 @@ DECLSPEC_ALIGN(64) ULONG64 __wine_d2r_server_calls[1032];
 
 /* d2r (patch 0009): latest caller per request type and completion port wait counters
